MID_EV30_029_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV30_029_m01_041: 
MID_EV30_029_m01_042: 
MID_EV30_029_m01_043: 
MID_EV30_029_m01_044: 
MID_EV30_029_m01_045: 
MID_EV30_029_m01_046: 
MID_EV30_029_m01_047: 
MID_EV30_029_m01_048: 
MID_EV30_029_m01_001: You've fought long and well. The time has come for\nthe battle that will decide this world's fate.
MID_EV30_029_m01_002: Our final task is to destroy the underworld gate in\nthe temple of Balor.
MID_EV30_029_m01_003: One gatekeeper remains. One barrier left to breach.
MID_EV30_029_m01_007: Then we can enter the underworld itself and reach\nBalor's lair.
MID_EV30_029_m01_008: Our path shall take us to his domain. 'Tis unknown\nterritory, even for me.
MID_EV30_029_m01_009: But I'll give my all and support you as best I'm able.
MID_EV30_029_m01_010: <NCA>"Victory will be ours."
MID_EV30_029_m01_040: 
MID_EV30_029_m01_011: Well, we made it this far.
MID_EV30_029_m01_012: And I don't care if Balor is my great-grandfather.\nWe're taking him down.
MID_EV30_029_m01_013: I never thought I'd have the fate of the world on\nmy shoulders...
MID_EV30_029_m01_014: Here, at least, let's hope we finish this. Honestly,\ntruly finish it.
MID_EV30_029_m01_015: Balor... When I think of him, my heart begins\nits dance.
MID_EV30_029_m01_016: Perhaps I will finally find the pleasure I have\nsought so relentlessly.
MID_EV30_029_m01_017: We may consider this a test to determine whether\nhumanity is capable of inheriting this world.
MID_EV30_029_m01_018: Let us pass it, then, that we may usher in an\nage of humans.
MID_EV30_029_m01_019: 
MID_EV30_029_m01_020: 
MID_EV30_029_m01_021: 
MID_EV30_029_m01_022: 
MID_EV30_029_m01_023: 
MID_EV30_029_m01_024: 
MID_EV30_029_m01_025: 
MID_EV30_029_m01_026: 
MID_EV30_029_m01_027: 
MID_EV30_029_m01_028: 
MID_EV30_029_m01_029: 
MID_EV30_029_m01_030: 
MID_EV30_029_m01_031: 
MID_EV30_029_m01_032: 
MID_EV30_029_m01_033: 
MID_EV30_029_m01_034: We have reached the tipping point. I have no\nwisdom left to impart to you.
MID_EV30_029_m01_035: Pit everything you have against Balor and put a stop\nto his onslaught.
MID_EV30_029_m01_036: Pit everything you have against Balor and put a stop\nto his onslaught.
MID_EV30_029_m01_037: Whether this land—this world—falls to ruin depends\non what you do next.
MID_EV30_029_m01_038: 'Tis in your hands now. Should you succeed, I vow\nthat we'll all make it back together.
MID_EV30_029_m01_039: Yes. You must not die until you have seen the fruits\nof this land's liberation from the underworld.
MID_EV30_030_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV30_030_m01_001: Ngh... Damn it. I'm fading again...
MID_EV30_030_m01_002: But I can't afford to collapse now. Not before I've\nperformed my final task.
MID_EV30_030_m01_003: Fortuna! Are you alright? You don't look well!
MID_EV30_030_m01_004: You... I forbid you to tell anyone of this.
MID_EV30_030_m01_005: This is a critical moment. I can't have anyone\ndistracted from the mission.
MID_EV30_030_m01_006: You're pushing yourself too hard. I've been\nconcerned about that for a while now.
MID_EV30_030_m01_007: You must have realized by now that I am no\ndaughter of Dagda's.
MID_EV30_030_m01_008: I'm one of her simulacra, dispatched to monitor\nthat lout Dagda and his domain.
MID_EV30_030_m01_009: Which is to say, I am on a higher level than the\nrest of you.
MID_EV30_030_m01_010: So spare me the unfounded concern. I'll not have you\nlump me in with the others.
MID_EV30_030_m01_011: Ah. I've long thought there was something different\nabout you.
MID_EV30_030_m01_012: I knew that Father was terrified of you—and that\nhe tried hard to stay at a distance.
MID_EV30_030_m01_013: You also broke a barrier made by a Founder. Few\nof her children should be capable of that.
MID_EV30_030_m01_014: 'Tis barely something her simulacrum is capable of,\nin truth.
MID_EV30_030_m01_015: I'm so drained that I ought to be hibernating now.
MID_EV30_030_m01_016: Fortuna... Perhaps, leave this to the others\nfor now? Rest a little.
MID_EV30_030_m01_017: If I rest, we risk losing everything we've fought for.\nI won't let their struggle go to waste!
MID_EV30_030_m01_018: But more than that...I don't want them to worry\nover nothing.
MID_EV30_030_m01_019: I've always thought you were the indifferent type.\nBut now, to these humans, you sound...considerate.
MID_EV30_030_m01_020: I assumed this was because of the progenitor\ngod's orders. It seems I was wrong.
MID_EV30_030_m01_021: Hmph! They're like babes in arms. They lack\nall sense and trip over themselves.
MID_EV30_030_m01_022: They need nursemaiding. I can't afford to take my\neyes off them.
MID_EV30_030_m01_023: So, you've come to...like humans, have you?
MID_EV30_030_m01_024: P-preposterous! What a thing to say.
MID_EV30_030_m01_025: What is there to like about them? Don't be absurd!
MID_EV30_030_m01_026: I'd better not find you spreading this rubbish to\nanyone else. Is that understood?!
MID_EV30_030_m01_027: Alright, alright. This stays between us. No need\nto get that upset.
MID_EV30_030_m01_028: Hehe. Really, who knew?
MID_EV30_031_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV30_031_m01_001: So you're finally here, Promised One. You are\nstronger than I calculated.
MID_EV30_031_m01_060: 
MID_EV30_031_m01_061: 
MID_EV30_031_m01_062: 
MID_EV30_031_m01_063: 
MID_EV30_031_m01_064: 
MID_EV30_031_m01_065: 
MID_EV30_031_m01_066: 
MID_EV30_031_m01_067: 
MID_EV30_031_m01_002: Alas... Aha... Hahaha.
MID_EV30_031_m01_003: <NCA>"What's so funny?"
MID_EV30_031_m01_004: You missed your window. It's too late to do\nanything now.
MID_EV30_031_m01_005: Before long, we'll see a total solar eclipse.
MID_EV30_031_m01_006: That will be Father's cue to soar out from the\nunderworld and destroy everything.
MID_EV30_031_m01_007: All that will be left is the underworld. It will\ncompletely replace this one.
MID_EV30_031_m01_008: Death and silence will rule over all. There won't be\na single living soul left.
MID_EV30_031_m01_009: So you say, but I have no intention of sitting idly by\nwhile this happens.
MID_EV30_031_m01_010: 
MID_EV30_031_m01_011: You're not like the other gatekeepers. You're\nnot dead.
MID_EV30_031_m01_012: 
MID_EV30_031_m01_013: 
MID_EV30_031_m01_014: 
MID_EV30_031_m01_015: Ah? Dietrich.
MID_EV30_031_m01_016: Lyrah! Here I stand, as I said I would.
MID_EV30_031_m01_017: Dietrich... My beloved...
MID_EV30_031_m01_018: If only you had accepted my love those years ago.
MID_EV30_031_m01_019: I might have cast it all aside and given all of myself\nto you.
MID_EV30_031_m01_020: It would be a different world today. I'm sure of it.
MID_EV30_031_m01_021: No. What matters is what has come to pass. Not\nwhat might have.
MID_EV30_031_m01_022: I am on this side. You are on the other. It is\nnow thus.
MID_EV30_031_m01_023: Ah! You are cruel, my love.
MID_EV30_031_m01_024: But that's what makes you the second man I've\never loved!
MID_EV30_031_m01_025: Now, let all living things reflect on the end before\nit comes.
MID_EV30_031_m01_026: Let them tremble in fear at the thought!
MID_EV30_031_m01_027: And no one, not even you, will prevent it.
MID_EV30_031_m01_028: My father's dearest wish was for revenge against the\nworld. That is everything to me.
MID_EV30_031_m01_029: 
MID_EV30_031_m01_030: 
MID_EV30_031_m01_031: 
MID_EV30_031_m01_032: 
MID_EV30_031_m01_033: 
MID_EV30_031_m01_034: 
MID_EV30_031_m01_035: 
MID_EV30_031_m01_036: 
MID_EV30_031_m01_037: 
MID_EV30_031_m01_038: 
MID_EV30_031_m01_039: 
MID_EV30_031_m01_040: 
MID_EV30_031_m01_041: 
MID_EV30_031_m01_042: 
MID_EV30_031_m01_043: 
MID_EV30_031_m01_044: 
MID_EV30_031_m01_045: 
MID_EV30_031_m01_046: 
MID_EV30_031_m01_047: 
MID_EV30_031_m01_048: 
MID_EV30_031_m01_049: Daughter of Balor, these wishes you hold so dear\nwill go unfulfilled.
MID_EV30_031_m01_050: The Promised One has come to lay waste to your\nfather's plans.
MID_EV30_031_m01_051: <NCA>"That's right."
MID_EV30_031_m01_052: Prattle on all you like, simulacrum. Is this Promised\nOne supposed to impress me?
MID_EV30_031_m01_053: I see only a makeshift Mediator of Nuwa.
MID_EV30_031_m01_054: No... What are you?
MID_EV30_031_m01_055: Have we met somewhere before?
MID_EV30_031_m01_056: Impossible. You're no mere Mediator. What are you\nplaying at?
MID_EV30_031_m01_057: Hm. Well, no matter.
MID_EV30_031_m01_058: Come for me, Promised One. I'll show you true fear.
MID_EV30_031_m01_059: Quiver before the power of Balor's children!
MID_EV30_032_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV30_032_m01_001: Don't you know...what's beyond this gate?
MID_EV30_032_m01_072: 
MID_EV30_032_m01_073: 
MID_EV30_032_m01_074: 
MID_EV30_032_m01_075: 
MID_EV30_032_m01_076: 
MID_EV30_032_m01_077: 
MID_EV30_032_m01_078: 
MID_EV30_032_m01_079: 
MID_EV30_032_m01_002: I cannot let you reach...my father...
MID_EV30_032_m01_003: You won't stop us, daughter of Balor. We're here to\nensure your father's vision never becomes reality.
MID_EV30_032_m01_004: By the progenitor god and my own true name,\nwe'll vanquish him.
MID_EV30_032_m01_005: No. Don't come any closer! I can't let anyone set\nfoot inside here...
MID_EV30_032_m01_006: *sob* Father... I tried to protect you.
MID_EV30_032_m01_007: You...you'll see me again at your side soon...
MID_EV30_032_m01_009: 
MID_EV30_032_m01_010: 
MID_EV30_032_m01_011: 
MID_EV30_032_m01_012: 
MID_EV30_032_m01_013: 
MID_EV30_032_m01_014: 
MID_EV30_032_m01_015: 
MID_EV30_032_m01_016: 
MID_EV30_032_m01_017: 
MID_EV30_032_m01_018: 
MID_EV30_032_m01_019: 
MID_EV30_032_m01_020: 
MID_EV30_032_m01_021: 
MID_EV30_032_m01_022: 
MID_EV30_032_m01_023: 
MID_EV30_032_m01_024: 
MID_EV30_032_m01_025: 
MID_EV30_032_m01_026: 
MID_EV30_032_m01_027: 
MID_EV30_032_m01_028: 
MID_EV30_032_m01_029: 
MID_EV30_032_m01_030: 
MID_EV30_032_m01_031: 
MID_EV30_032_m01_032: 
MID_EV30_032_m01_033: 
MID_EV30_032_m01_034: 
MID_EV30_032_m01_035: 
MID_EV30_032_m01_036: 
MID_EV30_032_m01_037: 
MID_EV30_032_m01_038: 
MID_EV30_032_m01_039: 
MID_EV30_032_m01_040: 
MID_EV30_032_m01_041: 
MID_EV30_032_m01_042: 
MID_EV30_032_m01_043: 
MID_EV30_032_m01_044: 
MID_EV30_032_m01_045: 
MID_EV30_032_m01_046: 
MID_EV30_032_m01_071: 
MID_EV30_032_m01_047: 
MID_EV30_032_m01_048: 
MID_EV30_032_m01_049: 
MID_EV30_032_m01_050: 
MID_EV30_032_m01_051: 
MID_EV30_032_m01_052: 
MID_EV30_032_m01_053: 
MID_EV30_032_m01_054: 
MID_EV30_032_m01_055: 
MID_EV30_032_m01_056: 
MID_EV30_032_m01_057: 
MID_EV30_032_m01_058: 
MID_EV30_032_m01_059: 
MID_EV30_032_m01_060: 
MID_EV30_032_m01_061: 
MID_EV30_032_m01_062: 
MID_EV30_032_m01_063: 
MID_EV30_032_m01_008: Hmmm.
MID_EV30_033_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV30_032_m01_064: Now then, allow me.
MID_EV30_033_m01_073: 
MID_EV30_033_m01_074: 
MID_EV30_033_m01_075: 
MID_EV30_033_m01_076: 
MID_EV30_033_m01_077: 
MID_EV30_033_m01_078: 
MID_EV30_033_m01_079: 
MID_EV30_033_m01_080: 
MID_EV30_032_m01_065: This final gate leads to Balor. As one might expect,\n'tis sturdier still than those before it.
MID_EV30_032_m01_066: To break its barrier will be a daunting task.
MID_EV30_032_m01_067: <NCA>"Is there anything I can do to help?"
MID_EV30_032_m01_068: I'm afraid not. But your presence here is welcome\nsupport in itself.
MID_EV30_032_m01_069: Let's say it would suffice if you fixed the sight of me\nfirmly in your mind.
MID_EV30_032_m01_070: Enough preamble. I shall begin.
MID_EV30_033_m01_001: HRAAAH! Haaah...haaah...haaah...
MID_EV30_033_m01_002: I knew there'd be no easy entry into his domain.\nThe barrier on this gate was...challenging.
MID_EV30_033_m01_004: <NCA>"Are you alright?"
MID_EV30_033_m01_005: <NCB>"You should rest."
MID_EV30_033_m01_006: <ACA>I may have forged a way through, but even I have\nmy limits.
MID_EV30_033_m01_007: <ACA>Still, no rest for the weary. We must go within and\ndestroy Balor.
MID_EV30_033_m01_008: <ACB>As if I could sit idly by after coming this far!
MID_EV30_033_m01_009: <ACB>I will be there with you when you see this matter\nthrough to its end.
MID_EV30_033_m01_010: Odd to find myself here at long last.
MID_EV30_033_m01_011: Hmm.
MID_EV30_033_m01_012: Before we enter... There is something you all\nmust know.
MID_EV30_033_m01_013: Listen carefully to what I tell you now, for your\nfutures are at stake.
MID_EV30_033_m01_014: When we step through that gate, we enter the depths\nof the underworld to destroy Balor.
MID_EV30_033_m01_015: But after his demise...we will be present in his\ndomain when it collapses.
MID_EV30_033_m01_016: So...what does that mean?
MID_EV30_033_m01_017: Put simply, I can't guarantee we'll escape with\nour lives.
MID_EV30_033_m01_018: Really?
MID_EV30_033_m01_019: A one-way ticket to the underworld without a\nguaranteed return. What a dream come true.
MID_EV30_033_m01_020: Mmm. I must say, I half suspected that might be\nthe case.
MID_EV30_033_m01_021: I'm sorry. I should have told you sooner than the\neleventh hour.
MID_EV30_033_m01_022: But I couldn't find the courage to say what needed\nto be said.
MID_EV30_033_m01_023: I... I care for you too much.
MID_EV30_033_m01_024: I owe you better than to send you unwittingly into\na battle with no return.
MID_EV30_033_m01_025: If any of you want to turn back here, no one could\nblame you.
MID_EV30_033_m01_026: Only those willing to brave the risks should take\nthe next step.
MID_EV30_033_m01_027: There is time for consideration. Think carefully on\nhow much you're willing to give.
MID_EV30_033_m01_081: 
MID_EV30_033_m01_082: 
MID_EV30_033_m01_029: Maybe I would've been wiser to keep the truth\nfrom them.
MID_EV30_033_m01_030: <NCA>"You did the right thing."
MID_EV30_033_m01_031: <NCB>"Have faith in them."
MID_EV30_033_m01_032: <ACA>Do you truly think so?
MID_EV30_033_m01_033: <ACA>The two of us confronting Balor alone is no more\npossible than pulling a mountain with a rope.
MID_EV30_033_m01_034: <ACB>I... I want to believe in them, of course.
MID_EV30_033_m01_035: <ACB>I can't very well dragoon them into the underworld\nkicking and screaming.
MID_EV30_033_m01_036: Argh...
MID_EV30_033_m01_037: We can't afford to wait forever. The solar eclipse is\nfast approaching.
MID_EV30_033_m01_038: <NCA>"Our wait is over."
MID_EV30_033_m01_039: Huh?
MID_EV30_033_m01_040: I've thought a lot about this, and here's how I see it.
MID_EV30_033_m01_041: If we don't go, ultimately the world's gonna\nend, right?
MID_EV30_033_m01_042: In that case, there's nowhere to hide. You saved my\nlife, Promised One. Let me put it to good use.
MID_EV30_033_m01_043: Let me be clear. I did not come here to die.
MID_EV30_033_m01_044: I hold out hope that even if the underworld does\ncollapse, we may find an escape.
MID_EV30_033_m01_045: I am willing to bet all on that hope. I have never\nwavered before, and I will not start now.
MID_EV30_033_m01_046: 
MID_EV30_033_m01_047: 
MID_EV30_033_m01_048: 
MID_EV30_033_m01_049: I don't want to go, to be honest. I'd like to keep my\nheart beating.
MID_EV30_033_m01_050: But Balor... He's too powerful.
MID_EV30_033_m01_051: Heh. Too powerful for you to handle without\nmy help, that is. So I'll be there.
MID_EV30_033_m01_052: 
MID_EV30_033_m01_053: 
MID_EV30_033_m01_054: 
MID_EV30_033_m01_055: 
MID_EV30_033_m01_056: 
MID_EV30_033_m01_057: 
MID_EV30_033_m01_058: Death has always been at my side. As ever, I do not\nfear it.
MID_EV30_033_m01_059: And if a foe will force me to wring out the last drop\nof my strength, so be it.
MID_EV30_033_m01_060: My pulse quickens...with a feeling more intense than\nI have known. I will not hesitate.
MID_EV30_033_m01_083: 
MID_EV30_033_m01_061: 
MID_EV30_033_m01_062: 
MID_EV30_033_m01_063: 
MID_EV30_033_m01_064: You came... You genuinely intend to go, despite\neverything?
MID_EV30_033_m01_065: Ah— Ha!
MID_EV30_033_m01_066: You fools... You absolute maniacs! This is so much\nmore than I dared hope.
MID_EV30_033_m01_067: But I am grateful for it. For all of you. Grateful,\nand so, so sorry.
MID_EV30_033_m01_068: <NCA>"Are you crying?"
MID_EV30_033_m01_069: These are tears of joy, I'll have you know. I... I...
MID_EV30_033_m01_070: I couldn't have asked for more wonderful companions\nthan you. My heart is full to know you.
MID_EV30_033_m01_071: Now come! Together, we venture into the\nunderworld and strike a final blow against Balor!
MID_EV30_033_m01_072: 
MID_EV30_034_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV30_034_m01_067: 
MID_EV30_034_m01_068: 
MID_EV30_034_m01_069: 
MID_EV30_034_m01_070: 
MID_EV30_034_m01_071: 
MID_EV30_034_m01_072: 
MID_EV30_034_m01_073: 
MID_EV30_034_m01_074: 
MID_EV30_034_m01_076: 
MID_EV30_034_m01_001: Rrrghhh...
MID_EV30_034_m01_002: A lowly band of living souls dares set foot in my\nunderworld?
MID_EV30_034_m01_003: Who would be so foolhardy?
MID_EV30_034_m01_004: <NCA>Give your name.
MID_EV30_034_m01_005: <NCB>"Never mind that, who are you?"
MID_EV30_034_m01_006: <ACA>Ahh... So you are the dullard calling yourself the\n"Promised One."
MID_EV30_034_m01_007: <ACB>I am Balor, king of this underworld. And soon I will\nrule over your world too.
MID_EV30_034_m01_008: It is about time you arrived here. You foolish\nmortals must learn your place.
MID_EV30_034_m01_009: He radiates cruelty and menace... I expected no less\nfrom our adversary.
MID_EV30_034_m01_010: Then this dragon is...my great-grandpa.
MID_EV30_034_m01_011: 
MID_EV30_034_m01_012: Ah! Hehehe... Ahahaha...
MID_EV30_034_m01_013: At last! I shall cast myself into battle with you and\nfall into rapture!
MID_EV30_034_m01_014: So we meet at last, the Darkest Dark.
MID_EV30_034_m01_015: I am Fortuna. The true name given to me by the\nprogenitor god is Voice upon the Peak.
MID_EV30_034_m01_017: Oh? Interesting. The progenitor god sent her\nsimulacrum, did she?
MID_EV30_034_m01_018: You're incorrigible. First you disobey her will,\nthen you hide yourself away in this grotesque lair.
MID_EV30_034_m01_019: Still nursing your grievance with her, I see. It's all\ntoo stupid for words.
MID_EV30_034_m01_020: You would do well to silence yourself in my presence.\nYou're nothing more than an empty vessel for her.
MID_EV30_034_m01_021: All that you strove for will come to nothing. My\npower is on the verge of perfection.
MID_EV30_034_m01_022: When I achieve that, I will fear nothing—not even\nyour vaunted progenitor god.
MID_EV30_034_m01_023: Really? You certainly have bravado to spare.
MID_EV30_034_m01_024: But sad to say, you have deluded yourself. For we\naim to nip this rebellion in the bud.
MID_EV30_034_m01_025: I ought to warn you not to take lightly those I've\ngathered here to destroy you.
MID_EV30_034_m01_026: So, you're the voice I've been hearing from\nObsidian, hm?
MID_EV30_034_m01_027: With the power that instrument's given me, I almost\nhate to say it... But we're going to end you here.
MID_EV30_034_m01_075: 
MID_EV30_034_m01_028: 
MID_EV30_034_m01_029: 
MID_EV30_034_m01_030: Silence! 
MID_EV30_034_m01_077: I will destroy all that is. In me is the end\nof everything.
MID_EV30_034_m01_031: You, who call yourself the Promised One. Do you\nseriously think you can stand against me?
MID_EV30_034_m01_032: The king of the underworld will not fall, no matter\nhow many lowly mortals challenge him.
MID_EV30_034_m01_033: Why risk your soul to fight me? For the pretty words\nof that vessel who leads you?
MID_EV30_034_m01_034: <NCA>"For the sake of the world and those living in it."
MID_EV30_034_m01_035: Hear, hear. The human world is a harsh place, and\nthe people's lives are seldom idyllic.
MID_EV30_034_m01_036: But they struggle onward anyway and cling fast to\nthe things they hold most dear.
MID_EV30_034_m01_037: All living things devote themselves fully to whatever\npurpose drives them.
MID_EV30_034_m01_038: If you are so twisted as to make your purpose their\neradication, I won't stand for it.
MID_EV30_034_m01_039: Ahh... Ludicrous. Absolutely ludicrous.
MID_EV30_034_m01_040: Yet you speak this to my face. Who has the audacity?
MID_EV30_034_m01_041: This rank insolence cannot have sprung from an\nordinary human.
MID_EV30_034_m01_042: <NCA>Remain silent.
MID_EV30_034_m01_043: You are an enigma to me. But very well...if you\ncame to face me, I shall oblige.
MID_EV30_034_m01_044: 
MID_EV30_034_m01_045: 
MID_EV30_034_m01_046: 
MID_EV30_034_m01_047: 
MID_EV30_034_m01_048: 
MID_EV30_034_m01_049: 
MID_EV30_034_m01_050: 
MID_EV30_034_m01_051: 
MID_EV30_034_m01_052: 
MID_EV30_034_m01_053: 
MID_EV30_034_m01_054: 
MID_EV30_034_m01_055: 
MID_EV30_034_m01_056: 
MID_EV30_034_m01_057: 
MID_EV30_034_m01_058: 
MID_EV30_034_m01_059: I will not be stopped. Not by you, and not by these\ninsects you have brought to swarm before me!
MID_EV30_034_m01_060: RRRAAAGH!
MID_EV30_034_m01_061: Pitiful. You've been reduced to something less than\na beast, incapable of reason.
MID_EV30_034_m01_062: Though even more terrifying are the rotten hearts\nof the dead, which drove even a Founder mad.
MID_EV30_034_m01_063: He's taken into himself all the poison in those\nsouls—all the resentment and hatred.
MID_EV30_034_m01_064: But we will not yield! I trust you all came prepared\nfor this fight.
MID_EV30_034_m01_065: <NCA>"It's ours to win."
MID_EV30_034_m01_066: Well said. 'Tis time for the showdown. To arms!
MID_EV30_035_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV30_035_m01_001: I'd hoped to see things through to the end...but I fear\nmy power is all but spent.
MID_EV30_035_m01_057: 
MID_EV30_035_m01_058: 
MID_EV30_035_m01_059: 
MID_EV30_035_m01_060: 
MID_EV30_035_m01_061: 
MID_EV30_035_m01_062: 
MID_EV30_035_m01_063: 
MID_EV30_035_m01_064: 
MID_EV30_035_m01_002: Is it... Is it finally over now? No...
MID_EV30_035_m01_065: 
MID_EV30_035_m01_003: 
MID_EV30_035_m01_004: C'mon, let's head back. I see no reason to stick\naround in this awful place.
MID_EV30_035_m01_005: Tsk.
MID_EV30_035_m01_006: My suspicions were correct, it seems. It still hasn't\neven begun.
MID_EV30_035_m01_007: <NCA>"What's wrong?"
MID_EV30_035_m01_008: Have you not realized? Take a good look around you.
MID_EV30_035_m01_009: What— But, why? Father died. I know he did.
MID_EV30_035_m01_010: The underworld has yet to collapse. What do you\nmake of that?
MID_EV30_035_m01_011: <NCA>"I don't know."
MID_EV30_035_m01_012: <NCB>"His true body is somewhere else?"
MID_EV30_035_m01_013: <ACA>Nor do I. What is going on here?
MID_EV30_035_m01_014: <ACB>What was that? What did you say?
MID_EV30_035_m01_015: Hm...
MID_EV30_035_m01_016: We know that the underworld is essentially\ncontained within Balor's soul.
MID_EV30_035_m01_017: Thus far, the inner self of Balor—the underworld—\ntouched our world in a very limited way.
MID_EV30_035_m01_018: The temple where Balor was sealed is one example.\nPlaces rife with the risen dead are another.
MID_EV30_035_m01_019: And we're all familiar with what happens when\npeople draw on the power of his remains.
MID_EV30_035_m01_020: These connections were tenuous things that naturally\nflickered out after a brief while.
MID_EV30_035_m01_021: But now the underworld has gained substance\nthrough Balor's incarnation.
MID_EV30_035_m01_022: Enough, it seems, to avoid collapse despite the\ndestruction of Balor's soul. It persists even now.
MID_EV30_035_m01_023: In which case...there should be something deeper\nsupporting this incarnation of the underworld.
MID_EV30_035_m01_024: A pillar for his domain, so to speak.
MID_EV30_035_m01_025: I believe we can go deeper inside through there.
MID_EV30_035_m01_026: The Promised One and I will go on alone. The rest\nof you should make your way outside.
MID_EV30_035_m01_027: But Balor's dead. Can't we just leave it be?
MID_EV30_035_m01_028: 
MID_EV30_035_m01_056: 
MID_EV30_035_m01_029: That is, unfortunately, out of the question.
MID_EV30_035_m01_031: The underworld is an innate part of Balor. 'Tis like\na simulacrum of him.
MID_EV30_035_m01_032: If we leave it be, a new Balor may be reborn from\nhis domain.
MID_EV30_035_m01_033: And so we cannot allow it to remain standing.
MID_EV30_035_m01_034: 'Tis hard to be certain of this without confirming\nmy theory first, but...
MID_EV30_035_m01_035: I suspect the entire underworld will collapse quickly\nonce its supporting pillar is destroyed.
MID_EV30_035_m01_036: This is a matter for those of us with ties to the\nprogenitor god. The Promised One and I will go.
MID_EV30_035_m01_037: I implore you all to leave before the underworld\ncollapses. Your own world awaits.
MID_EV30_035_m01_038: Go home to the people awaiting you there.
MID_EV30_035_m01_039: <NCA>"Don't worry about us."
MID_EV30_035_m01_055: 
MID_EV30_035_m01_040: 
MID_EV30_035_m01_041: So you have no plan to return from this.
MID_EV30_035_m01_042: Don't go, Promised One! Balor has been vanquished.\nThere is no need for you two to remain.
MID_EV30_035_m01_043: Fear not. I'll be assisting, as ever.
MID_EV30_035_m01_044: I won't know until we get there, but there's always\na chance we find our own escape.
MID_EV30_035_m01_045: And if we do...I doubt we'll have time to shepherd\na large force through it.
MID_EV30_035_m01_046: 
MID_EV30_035_m01_047: Hm. We must go.
MID_EV30_035_m01_048: Farewell, everyone. I'll always be grateful that you\nwould follow me even into the depths of hell.
MID_EV30_035_m01_049: Go. Live. There will come a day when your finite\nflame is snuffed.
MID_EV30_035_m01_050: So burn brightly until then, to ensure you pass on\nwithout regrets.
MID_EV30_035_m01_054: 
MID_EV30_035_m01_051: Are you ready?
MID_EV30_035_m01_052: <NCA>"Let's go."
MID_EV30_035_m01_053: Yes. We must settle all scores, with finality this time.
MID_EV30_041_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV30_041_m01_001: My goodness, but he's been busy. We've come to his\ninnards at last.
MID_EV30_041_m01_002: <NCA>"What do you mean?"
MID_EV30_041_m01_003: <NCB>"His innards?"
MID_EV30_041_m01_004: <ACA>The scale of his ambition is nigh unthinkable.
MID_EV30_041_m01_005: <ACB>Yes...the underworld was inside of him. Inside his\nnew body, I should say.
MID_EV30_041_m01_006: He wanted tremendous power, enough to rival that\nof the progenitor god.
MID_EV30_041_m01_007: And to gain it, he used the souls he snared to\nreshape the underworld itself.
MID_EV30_041_m01_008: He must have poured a long, long time and a\nstaggering number of souls into the project.
MID_EV30_041_m01_009: <NCA>"He was turning the underworld into a new body?"
MID_EV30_041_m01_010: Hmm.
MID_EV30_041_m01_011: Something about his scheme nagged at me from the\nvery beginning.
MID_EV30_041_m01_012: If his goal was to amass power and be revived,\nthere were easier ways of doing so.
MID_EV30_041_m01_013: Yet he and his daughters plotted for over a\nthousand years.
MID_EV30_041_m01_014: Their schemes drove men mad and ruined nations.\nIt did seem a strangely circuitous plan.
MID_EV30_041_m01_015: Granted, he had practically abandoned all reason,\nbut still.
MID_EV30_041_m01_016: I assumed if he meant to challenge her again,\nhe had some strategy in place.
MID_EV30_041_m01_017: And now I find 'twas all to prepare a vessel truly\ncapable of opposing the progenitor god!
MID_EV30_041_m01_018: In that light...the thing ready to manifest at the next\nsolar eclipse would have been...
MID_EV30_041_m01_019: Damn it all!
MID_EV30_041_m01_020: I had thought that, if things grew dire, I could seal\nthe underworld with my power. How naïve I was!
MID_EV30_041_m01_021: Listen to me! This absolutely must not be allowed\nto exist.
MID_EV30_041_m01_022: If some evil soul should chance to find this body\nand claim it...
MID_EV30_041_m01_023: it could emerge into the world at the solar eclipse\nand destroy all life.
MID_EV30_041_m01_024: We must be certain that we destroy it now, even at\nthe cost of our lives!
MID_EV30_037_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV30_037_m01_001: 'Tis about time you awakened.
MID_EV30_037_m01_002: <NCA>"What is this place?"
MID_EV30_037_m01_003: We were caught up in the underworld's collapse.\nThis is where we find ourselves as a result.
MID_EV30_037_m01_004: 'Tis not the underworld. No, this is a place of perfect\nemptiness. Neither time nor space hold sway here.
MID_EV30_037_m01_005: Most would have died in the collapse. Fortunately,\nour unique hearts prevented that.
MID_EV30_037_m01_006: Though 'tis an open question whether "fortunate" is\nthe best word for our situation.
MID_EV30_037_m01_007: You had a grim role to play, and played it to the last.
MID_EV30_037_m01_008: And I... Although 'twas necessary, I'm sorry you had\nto come along with me.
MID_EV30_037_m01_009: Though I do have a soft spot for hapless fools like\nyou who bumble their way through life.
MID_EV30_037_m01_010: I've decided. This time and this time only, I'll tip the\nscales in your favor.
MID_EV30_037_m01_011: <NCA>"What does that mean?"
MID_EV30_037_m01_012: It means I'll use what power I have left in me to get\nyou out of this space.
MID_EV30_037_m01_013: Though if that isn't enough, I may have to borrow\nsome power from your heart.
MID_EV30_037_m01_014: But I think between the two of us, there is enough\nto return you to the world.
MID_EV30_037_m01_015: <NCA>"But what about you?"
MID_EV30_037_m01_016: Hmm...
MID_EV30_037_m01_017: I'll rest in this space until I recover enough strength\nfor my own exit.
MID_EV30_037_m01_018: Don't you worry. Even Balor originally came out of\nthe chaos within the progenitor god.
MID_EV30_037_m01_019: A creature like me, with such close ties to her,\ncould never vanish. Not even from this nothingness.
MID_EV30_037_m01_020: This war has exhausted my power, but never fear.\n'Twill return in time. And then so will I.
MID_EV30_037_m01_021: But I doubt you and I will meet again in this life.
MID_EV30_037_m01_022: Even when I do escape, there is no telling where\nI will emerge.
MID_EV30_037_m01_023: And never mind where—there is also the when.\nI could return into a completely different era.
MID_EV30_037_m01_024: Or I may not escape. 'Tis possible my strength fails\nme in the attempt and I return to the progenitor god.
MID_EV30_037_m01_025: Looking back, I have lived a rather long life.
MID_EV30_037_m01_026: The progenitor god assigned me as Dagda's minder\nabout two thousand years ago.
MID_EV30_037_m01_027: I came to this land as Dagda's daughter, hiding my\ntrue origin, and languished here for a long time.
MID_EV30_037_m01_028: She charged me with watching over this land and\nits gradual development.
MID_EV30_037_m01_029: I was also to ensure that humans never again do\nanything to awaken the progenitor god's true self.
MID_EV30_037_m01_030: Yet she forbade me from interfering in events unless\na crisis arose.
MID_EV30_037_m01_031: So I didn't concern myself with the trivialities that\nmake up human lives.
MID_EV30_037_m01_032: I spent many days of boredom observing the\npanicked thrashing of that lout Dagda.
MID_EV30_037_m01_033: I stayed at a remove from human causality,\nrationalizing that such was my lot in life.
MID_EV30_037_m01_034: But my travels with you were fun.
MID_EV30_037_m01_035: I fulfilled my duty, and the people I spent so much\ntime with were a delightful bunch.
MID_EV30_037_m01_036: You lived up to your role as the Promised One. Now,\nyour life should be yours to spend as you see fit.
MID_EV30_037_m01_037: And to get you started, I'll send you to the person\nyou most dearly long to see.
MID_EV30_037_m01_038: Consider it a parting gift from the Goddess of Fate.
MID_EV30_037_m01_039: So tell me...who do you want to return to?
MID_EV30_037_m01_068: <RS>
MID_EV30_037_m01_040: You're certain?
MID_EV30_037_m01_041: <NCA>"I'm certain."
MID_EV30_037_m01_042: <NCB>Reconsider.
MID_EV30_037_m01_069: <ACB>
MID_EV30_037_m01_043: <ACA>Then picture the person you seek. Focus on them\nwith all your heart!
MID_EV30_037_m01_044: <ACA>The image still isn't clear enough for me to send you\nto them! Do you want this or not?!
MID_EV30_037_m01_045: <ACA>There! 'Tis coming into focus. I've almost got it...\ndon't let your concentration slip now!
MID_EV30_037_m01_046: <ACA>Wh... What?!
MID_EV30_037_m01_047: <ACA>Me, of all people?! This is no time for jokes.
MID_EV30_037_m01_048: <ACA>Do you not understand your situation? If you go now,\nyou can still get out in time!
MID_EV30_037_m01_049: <ACA>H-has the emptiness of this place sapped you of\nyour wits? Hahaha!
MID_EV30_037_m01_050: <ACA>Hahaha... Ha... *sniffle*
MID_EV30_037_m01_051: <ACA>Could you...really have meant that?
MID_EV30_037_m01_052: <NCA>"It wasn't a joke."
MID_EV30_037_m01_053: Ah... Ah?!
MID_EV30_037_m01_054: *sob*
MID_EV30_037_m01_055: In all my life, no one has ever wanted me like this.
MID_EV30_037_m01_056: I've always been lonely.
MID_EV30_037_m01_057: I told myself that I had to stay isolated, due to the\ntask the progenitor god set me.
MID_EV30_037_m01_058: So I never grew close with anyone. Not in the holy\nland nor in your land.
MID_EV30_037_m01_059: But... You have no idea how comforting your\npresence has been to me in this campaign.
MID_EV30_037_m01_060: I thought to myself that I was saving you.
MID_EV30_037_m01_061: But now...I believe you were my savior instead.
MID_EV30_037_m01_062: You were the rock that kept me steady through our\nlong war.
MID_EV30_037_m01_063: I think...I understand better now. The moment when\nshe, too, opened her heart to a single human.
MID_EV30_037_m01_064: It must have felt something like this.
MID_EV30_037_m01_065: As you wish, then. Let us continue on together\nforever—to wherever this causality takes us.
MID_EV30_037_m01_066: Hey. I...
MID_EV30_037_m01_067: No...never mind.
MID_EV30_037_m01_070: Thank you for everything.
MID_NR30_01_m01: <SH>
MID_NR30_01_m01_001: The tangled threads of causality came undone at\nlong last, slipping quietly into the flow of time.
MID_NR30_01_m01_002: The darkness hanging over the continent vanished.\nThe light of the sun shone upon people again.
MID_NR30_01_m01_003: With the calamity wrought by Balor now over, the\nland of Dagda welcomed an age of rebirth.
MID_NR30_01_m01_004: As war turned to peace, many survivors were\neager to return to their homelands.
MID_NR30_01_m01_005: Some of them sought to bring calm to the chaos\nstill found across the entire continent.
MID_NR30_01_m01_006: Others longed for the warmth and love of their\nfamilies, who yearned for their return.
MID_NR30_01_m01_007: And so ended the immense struggle that future\nhistorians would come to call the Underworld War.
MID_NR30_01_m01_008: Yet as the curtains closed on this event, its central\nfigure, the Promised One, remained missing, and\nwas presumed lost in the underworld...
MID_NR30_01_m01_009: —Saint Cichol, "The Underworld War,"\nPart 3, Chapter 6
