MID_NR30_99_m01: <SH>
MID_NR30_99_m01_001: So then. I see at last you have\ncome crawling back to me.
MID_NR30_99_m01_002: Your daughters thumbed their nose at my commands,\ndoing as they pleased—and so did you.
MID_NR30_99_m01_005: It seems a willful heart cannot be tamed. Infuriating,\nbut that is the way of living things.
MID_NR30_99_m01_006: Hmhm. Oh, fear me not. The past is past.\nHey! You'll heed me when I speak to you.
MID_NR30_99_m01_008: Did I just hear you beg me to forgive? Hm. No sooner\nasked than done.
MID_NR30_99_m01_009: If I cannot forgive such foolishness, who else in all\nthe world could be so kind?
MID_NR30_99_m01_011: Hmhm. Your sentence is to drown in Mother's\nlove—a vaster depth than any of the seas.
MID_NR30_99_m01_012: Hehehe. I think it fitting for a child at rest to\nhear a bedtime story as you doze.
MID_NR30_99_m01_013: I'll tell my tale, but where to start? Aha. A long,\nlong time ago...
MID_NR30_99_m01_014: Back at the time I first left that twinkling blue star,\nand took to wandering the celestial sea...